                <pb facs="0737" n="712" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v08/pg712"/>

                <head>307. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The Foreign Ministers did not meet on Saturday May 16 or Sunday May 17. Secretary
                    of State Herter took advantage of this hiatus to fly to Rome on May 16 for
                    conversations with Prime Minister Segni and Foreign Minister Pella. During the
                    course of a meeting at the Villa Madama from 1:30 to 4:30 p.m., Herter briefed
                    the Italian leaders on the first week of the Foreign Ministers Conference and
                    explained the Western Peace Plan in some detail. A memorandum of this
                    conversation, US/MC/24, is in Department of State, Conference Files: Lot 64 D
                    560, CF 1350.</p>
            </div>
